      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (en): Cyclanthera brachystachya § Cultivation",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyclanthera_brachystachya#Cultivation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1342448481,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "It is propagated by its puzzle-piece-shaped seed, and grown in conditions similar to other cucurbits like cucumbers and melons. It prefers warm to hot climates with regular watering. Once established the vine can grow quickly up to 3–5 m. Although preferably grown over some kind of support, it can also be grown along the ground.\n\n■ Food uses\nThe fruit can be used raw when small (less than 2 cm) in salads, or cooked when mature (2.5 cm, exploded).",
        "truncated": false
      }
